# phaze — .dockerignore
#
# ONE build context for every image: every Dockerfile is built with `context: .`
# (docker-compose.yml, .github/workflows/docker-{validate,publish}.yml), so this
# single file governs the api/worker image and the arm64 agent image.
#
# ALLOWLIST, not denylist. The previous denylist had drifted badly — .beads/
# (Dolt store + .beads-credential-key), .repowise/, .worktrees/, .bv/, .mcp.json,
# .envrc and certs/ (which holds the phaze-ca.key / phaze-server.key private keys
# generated by phaze.cert_bootstrap) were all being uploaded to the daemon. None
# is COPYed by any Dockerfile, so none was ever baked into an image, but they do
# not belong in the context. Denying-by-default means the next new top-level
# directory is excluded automatically instead of leaking until someone notices.
#
# To add a path here you must have a matching COPY. Current COPY inventory:
#   Dockerfile ................ assets/ src/ alembic/ alembic.ini pyproject.toml uv.lock
#   Dockerfile.agent-arm64 .... src/ alembic/ alembic.ini pyproject.toml uv.lock
#   Dockerfile.job ............ (none — FROM ${BASE_IMAGE} only)

# Exclude everything...
*

# ...then re-include exactly what the COPY lines above need.
!alembic/
!alembic.ini
!assets/
!pyproject.toml
!src/
!uv.lock

# Derived and machine-local junk that lives *inside* the re-included trees.
# Without these, the per-package __pycache__/ dirs would ride back in through
# `!src/`.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[codz]
**/.venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Generated by the css-builder stage and COPYed --from it at Dockerfile:76. A
# stale local copy (from `just tailwind`) would otherwise bust the cache on
# `COPY src/ src/` without changing the final image.
src/phaze/static/css/app.css
